### Design Rationale

| Milestone | Rule Type | Why This Rule | Why Not Alternatives |
|-----------|-----------|---------------|---------------------|
| mine_oak_door | `inventory_has(oak_door, 1)` | Door drops as item into inventory when mined in survival | `mine_block` would also work but `inventory_has` is preferred per guidelines; `position_inside_box` would be wrong since this isn't a navigation task |
| craft_oak_button | `inventory_has(oak_button, 1)` | Crafted button goes directly to inventory | `craft_item` counter would also work but `inventory_has` is the preferred first-choice for craft tasks |

Both milestones are minimal (single rule each), directly checkable, and impossible to satisfy without completing the intended task. The dependency is enforced spatially by the scene (door blocks access to crafting materials), not by the milestone rules themselves — which is the correct design pattern.
